From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joan Karadimov <joan.karadimov@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:40:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Tell 64-bit Windows from the pointer size

DetectMachine takes 64-bit Windows from a WIN64 variable that only the
MinGW cross toolchain files set. A native x86_64 build is detected as
32-bit, and RemoteVstPlugin then returns the address of its VstTimeInfo
to VST plugins through a 32-bit long. Treat an 8-byte pointer as 64-bit
Windows too.

Upstream: not submitted
---
 cmake/modules/DetectMachine.cmake | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/cmake/modules/DetectMachine.cmake b/cmake/modules/DetectMachine.cmake
index 924b59c..2a4aa77 100644
--- a/cmake/modules/DetectMachine.cmake
+++ b/cmake/modules/DetectMachine.cmake
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@ SET(LMMS_HOST_X86 FALSE)
 SET(LMMS_HOST_X86_64 FALSE)
 
 IF(WIN32)
-	IF(WIN64)
+	IF(WIN64 OR CMAKE_SIZEOF_VOID_P EQUAL 8)
 		SET(IS_X86_64 TRUE)
 		SET(LMMS_BUILD_WIN64 TRUE)
 	ELSE(WIN64)
